  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"An artist book by Werner Pfeiffer in memory of the victims of 9-11"--Leaf [1].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Published in 2006 ... to commemorate the fifth anniversary of 9-11"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 52 signed and numbered by the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"A three-dimensional book consisting of a group of large woodcuts in the shape of two towers, each over five feet tall"--Leaf [8].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in a folded case with three compartments.  Includes 14 illustrated boxes that open up to form two towers when assembled by the reader.  The base of each assembled tower fits into the compartment in which its components are stored.  The center compartment includes the eight-leaf book and the paper panels that open to fit inside the boxes and make them square.  Includes instructions for constructing the towers.</subfield>
